	'how_s4_p1' => 'Fitting is one day per standard bay up to 5 m wide. Wider openings, and fire-rated openings, take two fitting days. We close one bay at a time so you can keep loading. The crew that measured the bay is the crew that fits it. Joel Asante leads the fitting.',
	'how_s4_p2' => 'At Harbour Lane Cold Store, three insulated sectional doors took three days because one bay stayed closed at a time. At Corrie & Sons Hardware, a manual shopfront shutter changed to electric was fitted in one day before opening time. The old door is removed and recycled as part of the fitting, not as a later extra.',
	'how_s5_p1' => 'An aftercare visit is included at 12 months with every fitted door. Lena Brandt books it from the service desk. It is separate from a yearly service visit, which is from €140 per door and covers inspection, lubrication, adjustment and a report.',
	'how_s5_p2' => 'Emergency call-outs, for a shutter stuck open or shut, are the same day within 25 km, Monday to Saturday, 7:00 to 19:00, at €120. The call-out is not a substitute for the aftercare visit, and it is not included in the door price. Book it by phone on 021 480 1948.',
